  "configuration_id": "config_051",
  "reason": "Evidence: The strongest performance driver identified so far is the multiprofile + avgpool setting (config_044: 0.629 vs config_016 single-profile: 0.535), with pca_n2000 + imagenet_vit_l + concat as the best-known encoder/fusion combination. RNA encoder choice has shown the largest single-variable effect (pca_n2000 vs scgpt: ~10% gap in single-profile), yet scvi_n200 remains completely untested across all experiments. Question: config_051 isolates the effect of switching the RNA encoder from pca_n2000 to scvi_n200 while holding all other components at their empirically best settings (multiprofile, imagenet_vit_l, avgpool, concat). This tests whether a learned nonlinear variational representation captures cell-type structure that linear PCA misses, particularly under multiprofile aggregation where richer per-profile embeddings may benefit more from nonlinear compression. Why best next experiment: It changes exactly one variable (RNA encoder) from the current best configuration, directly addresses the largest remaining uncertainty (untested encoder class), and has high potential upside if scvi_n200 outperforms PCA. A negative result would also be informative, confirming PCA's sufficiency and redirecting effort toward other axes."
}

